<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fu Jian (337–385)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">337–385</span> · Also known as Fu Jian of Former Qin, Emperor Xuanzhao of Former Qin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fu Jian was the Di ruler of the Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> from 357, served by the able minister Wang Meng. He conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/former-yan">Former Yan</a>, Former Liang and Dai, unifying northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 376. His invasion of the southern Eastern Jin ended in disaster at the Battle of the Fei River in 383, after which his empire broke apart, and he was killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yao-chang">Yao Chang</a> in 385.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fu-jian-337-385.jpg" alt="Fu Jian (337–385)" width="320" height="507" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: see below · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harvard_drs_49802792_%E7%B9%A1%E5%83%8F%E4%B8%89%E5%9C%8B%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E7%BA%8C%E7%B7%A8_v.1_(%E8%8B%BB%E5%A0%85).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
